Feature Translation: When AI Enters the Harness Era: MiniMax as a Case Stud=
y for the New Cloud Infrastructure of AI Agents [ https://substack.com/redi=
rect/888b5405-265c-4492-b00d-66b04cf41836?j=3DeyJ1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_GWC=
zChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E ]
Context: In February, a small OpenAI team disclosed the results of a five-m=
onth experiment: =E2=80=9Cbuilding and shipping an internal beta of a softw=
are product with 0 lines of manually-written code [ https://substack.com/re=
direct/746fd728-b325-4392-b5a1-9f328e9eff3e?j=3DeyJ1IjoiMmZseDYifQ.6O_iC1_G=
WCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E ].=E2=80=9D Using OpenAI=E2=80=99s soft=
ware engineering agent Codex, the three person-team used a =E2=80=9Charness=
 engineering=E2=80=9D approach, summed up in four words: =E2=80=9CHumans st=
eer. Agents execute.=E2=80=9D In this world, human AI engineering skills ha=
ve shifted from merely designing context-rich or helpful prompts:
=E2=80=9COur most difficult challenges now center on designing environments=
, feedback loops, and control systems that help agents accomplish our goal=
=E2=80=A6=E2=80=9D
In this week=E2=80=99s feature translation of a jiqizhixin  [ https://subst=
ack.com/redirect/97cdff2f-6493-4b17-95bb-7b8e94ad3f20?j=3DeyJ1IjoiMmZseDYif=
Q.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E ](Synced) article [ https://s=
ubstack.com/redirect/97cdff2f-6493-4b17-95bb-7b8e94ad3f20?j=3DeyJ1IjoiMmZse=
DYifQ.6O_iC1_GWCzChnbrHzSrs1hMpJpoODTUJm_FAk3tf6E ], we dig into how Chines=
e companies are adapting to the Harness era. This article focuses on an int=
eresting partnership between the Chinese AI start-up MiniMax=E2=80=99s AI a=
gent (MaxClaw) and Alibaba Cloud.
Key Takeaways: MiniMax=E2=80=99s MaxClaw agent is in the first tier of Open=
Claw-based adaptations, but how does it deal with fundamental engineering b=
arriers? Remember, the Harness approach gives AI agents significant autonom=
y and access to high-risk privileges.
The article describes the core problem set: =E2=80=9CWhen hundreds of thous=
ands of agents concurrently execute these complex tasks with highly strict =
access privileges and multiple steps, traditional system architectures freq=
uently struggle to cope=E2=80=A6How does MiniMax manage to withstand the ma=
ssive traffic surges generated by MaxClaw and MaxHermes while ensuring busi=
ness stability?=E2=80=9D
Synced highlights four =E2=80=9Cchasms=E2=80=9D that limit the diffusion of=
 AI agents into enterprise-grade production environments: 1) security bound=
aries =E2=80=94 since agents are increasingly running directly on top of lo=
cal operating systems, they have high-risk privileges (e.g., deleting key f=
iles); 2) state volatility involved in executing long-running tasks; 3) nee=
d for scheduling multiple agents; and 4) tension between cost consumption a=
nd drastic workload fluctuations.
Enter MiniMax=E2=80=99s partnership with Alibaba Cloud=E2=80=99s Container =
Service for Kubernetes (ACK) and Container Compute Service (ACS), which tri=
es to address those four engineering challenges associated with large-scale=
 harnessing of agents.
On the security challenges, Agent execution occurs in the ACS Agent Sandbox=
, which isolates and contains the risk of prompt injection or privilege esc=
alation attacks. Per Synced, =E2=80=9Cthe scope of the resulting risk is st=
rictly contained within that specific instance, making lateral movement or =
container escape extremely difficult.=E2=80=9D
To handle unpredictable computational demands =E2=80=94 AI agents sometimes=
 have relatively idle periods, punctuated by sudden spikes of  workload =E2=
=80=94 Alibaba Cloud supports elastic scheduling of compute.
MiniMax=E2=80=99s evolution points toward the importance of cloud computing=
 platforms as =E2=80=9CAI super computers.=E2=80=9D
Citing an IDC survey that finds AI inference accounts for 47% of all token =
usage and API calls, the article notes that the AI industry is undergoing =
=E2=80=9Ctransition into a phase of large-scale post-training and inference=
 execution, as the focus of computing power rapidly shifts toward Agent-cen=
tric scenarios.=E2=80=9D
If enterprises collectively operate hundreds of thousands of AI agents, rou=
nd-the-clock seven days a week, then cloud computing platforms and modern c=
ontainer services like Alibaba Cloud=E2=80=99s ACK and ACS will serve as =
=E2=80=9Ccloud-native operating systems=E2=80=9D for AI supercomputers.
